  "id": "recipe-flux2-klein-4b.masked-edit",
  "revision": 1,
  "title": "FLUX.2 Klein 4B: edit inside a mask",
  "description": "Edits the masked area of a source image as the prompt instructs, with the distilled FLUX.2 Klein 4B: the source, scaled to the task's width and height, is encoded, given to the instruction as a ReferenceLatent and used as the sampling latent with the mask as its noise mask, so only the masked area is sampled anew (4 steps, CFG 1.0); ImageCompositeMasked then puts the result over the scaled source, so the pixels outside the mask are the source's. The output has the task's size; a soft check reports when the aspect ratios differ, since source and mask would be stretched. The mask is a separate image in ComfyUI's input folder, white where the image is repainted, read from its red channel by LoadImageMask. No Klein template has a mask: the masked path is this recipe's, after the inpaint pattern of upstream's comfyui-core skill.",
  "kind": "image",
  "operations": [
    "inpaint"
  ],
